{% comment %}
  TRMNL full-screen panel: the ongoing chess.com Daily game. 800x480, 1-bit.

  Both players paste this same file into their own private plugin; everything
  that differs between their panels (orientation, whose move "yours" is) arrives
  already decided in the merge variables from chess_panel.board.

  The board is drawn here as inline SVG rather than sent as an image: squares is
  a 64-character string in display order, walked with Liquid's slice. Pieces are
  the Cburnett set (as shipped by python-chess; GPLv2+/BSD/GFDL), defined once as
  symbols. Dark squares are a diagonal hatch rather than grey, since mid-tones
  dither badly at 1 bit; the last move is a heavy inset outline on both squares.
{% endcomment %}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Barlow+Condensed:wght@600;800&amp;family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;600&amp;display=swap">
<div class="view view--full">
  <div style="width: 800px; height: 480px; box-sizing: border-box; background: #ffffff; color: #000000; display: flex; font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', ui-monospace, 'DejaVu Sans Mono', monospace; -webkit-font-smoothing: none;">

    <svg viewBox="0 0 480 480" width="480" height="480" style="display: block; flex-shrink: 0;" aria-label="Chess board">
      <defs>
        <pattern id="dark" width="6" height="6" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse" patternTransform="rotate(45)">
          <rect width="6" height="6" fill="#ffffff"></rect>
          <rect width="2" height="6" fill="#000000"></rect>
        </pattern>
